    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "48e73de649cf537759253421b5500754bfd37566",
      "message": "OTA-1849 \u2014 lore and fallen share the row\n\nThe exploration card's right column stacked four things inside a 165px\nminimum: \u2691 WORLD, the live mini-map, \u25c8 LORE and \u2617 FALLEN. The last two are\nboth secondary destinations a player opens between fights, and the second of\nthem was spending a whole row of that column on a control reached once a run.\n\nPaired on one row at equal width they hand the row back to the mini-map,\nwhich is already `flex: 1` and absorbs it \u2014 no height is written anywhere,\nso the map is not resized by hand, it is simply given more room.\n\nPRESENTATION ONLY. Same TButton at the same `utility` variant and `compact`\ndensity, so the rim, face, press depression and reduce-motion behaviour are\nthe control they already were. Same labels, same handlers, same destinations,\nsame tap-ledger entries. Two style keys carry the whole change: `crestNavRow`\n(flexDirection + the named gutter) and `crestNavHalf` (flex: 1, minWidth: 0).\n\n`minWidth: 0` is load-bearing, not decoration: without it a flex child in a\nrow refuses to shrink below its text's intrinsic width, and the pair would\npush past the column's right edge instead of dividing it.\n\nTHE WIDTH IS ARITHMETIC, done for the narrowest supported device \u2014 iPhone\nSE 3 at 375pt:\n\n    375 \u2212 16 (container padding)          = 359\n    (359 \u2212 6 topRow gap) / 2              = 176.5  rightCol\n    176.5 \u2212 2 (panelFrame border)         = 174.5  inner\n    (174.5 \u2212 CREST_NAV_ROW_GAP) / 2       =  84.25 per key\n    84.25 \u2212 2 (btnRim) \u2212 16 (compact pad) =  66.25 text box\n\n\u26a0 AND THE MARGIN IS SMALL, SAID PLAINLY RATHER THAN ASSERTED AWAY.\n`\u2617 FALLEN` is eight characters at 10pt/800 with 1.8 letterSpacing \u2014 roughly\n63pt against that 66.25pt. Jest has no text shaper and the device fonts are\nnot in CI, so the suite proves the SLOT and the NO-WRAP guarantee and states\nthe glyph estimate as its floor; it does not pretend to have measured a\ntypeface. The label keeps the kit's numberOfLines={1}, so the worst case on a\ndevice whose fallback glyph for \u2617 runs wider than a square em is an ellipsis\non one line \u2014 never a wrapped or reflowed row. Hardware check outstanding.\n\nNew suite ota1849LoreAndFallenShareTheRow, 27 tests: row membership, the\nequal split, the absence of flexWrap, the arithmetic across every device in\nDEVICE_PROFILES, a render-level check that both keys resolve to the same flex\nand both labels are single-line, and six pins that the repair stopped at\npresentation. Its helpers are total on purpose \u2014 restoring the stacked column\nturns seven NAMED tests red instead of aborting the file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
